WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.604
- All right y'all we're
gonna finish things up

00:00:02.604 --> 00:00:03.479
with one last story

00:00:03.479 --> 00:00:04.410
I'm hoping you'll enjoy as much as I do.

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:05.610
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:06.469 --> 00:00:08.820
(Upbeat music)

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.460
It's remarkable how little
of a filter kids have

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:12.960
before they speak.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.150
Case in point, check out
this third grade teacher

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:16.260
instructing her students

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.381
on the basics of title abbreviations.

00:00:19.381 --> 00:00:21.325
- Mrs.

00:00:21.325 --> 00:00:23.670
So not to be confused with,
Mrs. is when someone's married

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:27.780
but I use Ms. because Ms. can be either/or

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.460
you could say the person's not married or-

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:30.960
- [Child 2] Why you not a Mrs?

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:32.910
- You know I'm not married.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:34.035
- [Child 1] Oh.

00:00:34.035 --> 00:00:34.868
- [Several Students] Oh.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:36.060
- [Child 2] Why you have
to do her like that?

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.530
You know her situation.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:40.523
- [Child 3] Miss Jasmine,
you will never be one.

00:00:40.523 --> 00:00:42.038
- [Child 2] Okay. First of all,

00:00:42.038 --> 00:00:43.320
I'm not even gonna check you right now,

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:44.951
because I know Ms. Evans

00:00:44.951 --> 00:00:46.060
gonna make you read a book-

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:47.145
- [Child 1] Read a book!

00:00:47.145 --> 00:00:48.430
- [Child 2] So you might
want to check yourself, sir.

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:50.460
- (laughing) Oh, my God.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:51.510
- I don't know what's funnier,

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.190
The fact that they were all like "Ooh"

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.110
or how defensive the kids were for her.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:56.310
It was amazing.

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:57.870
Probably why that video has racked up

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.030
more than 2 million views on TikTok.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:02.670
Luckily the teacher,
Jasmine, has a good sense

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:04.080
of humor about the whole thing.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.090
And we have her on the
line right now watching

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:08.190
on NBC5, Dallas Fort Worth.

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:09.879
What's up Jasmine?

00:01:09.879 --> 00:01:11.525
- [Crowd] Ooh! (applauding).

00:01:11.525 --> 00:01:13.440
- Hello, Kelly.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:14.940
- [Kelly Clarkson] Oh my
God, are your students

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:16.830
always that sassy?

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.081
- Yes.

00:01:18.081 --> 00:01:18.914
- (laughing)

00:01:18.914 --> 00:01:21.360
- They're, I have a big,
full of personality,

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:22.980
bunch of students.

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.590
I know that they're gonna go far in life,

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:27.780
because they have a
lot to offer the world.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:30.300
And, I started recording my lessons

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.710
to share with their parents.

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:34.057
And I get a mixture
between the parents saying,

00:01:34.057 --> 00:01:35.880
"oh my gosh, is that my kid?"

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.800
and "oh, that's my kid!"

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:41.310
And so, from the parents
my own friends and family

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:42.870
not believing me,

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:46.240
it's nice to see that the
world can see what I deal with,

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:47.610
what I've been dealing with,

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:50.580
and my experiences for the
past five years as a teacher.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:51.420
- Oh my gosh. I know.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:52.680
God bless you first of all.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:56.040
Being a teacher, the patience
of Job is what y'all have.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:58.650
So, they all really reacted
to you not being married.

00:01:58.650 --> 00:01:59.910
So do you think they really cared?

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:03.234
Because there were kids in
there that got mad for you.

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:04.904
- No, I think it's,

00:02:04.904 --> 00:02:07.387
we have a way of having
little playful banter

00:02:07.387 --> 00:02:10.750
between our lessons
and I don't think they.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.470
They have a lot of love for me and

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:15.990
we can have those interactions and

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.360
I think at the end of
the day, I love the kids.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:19.250
I love that.

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:20.913
I know that they're learning.

00:02:21.926 --> 00:02:25.420
We have those times where I can
humanize myself as a teacher

00:02:26.299 --> 00:02:28.260
and at the end of the day,
they feel comfortable with me.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:29.640
They come to me and they tell me

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.522
probably more than they should,

00:02:31.522 --> 00:02:33.750
but I like having that
line of of communication

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:35.858
open with them. They trust me, you know.

00:02:35.858 --> 00:02:37.350
- And that's awesome.

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:39.300
That's amazing that kids have that.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:40.350
My kids have been fortunate

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.420
to have amazing teachers
and I did as well.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:43.710
Thank you so much, Jasmine.

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:45.610
I'm liking your post right now, right?

00:02:46.682 --> 00:02:48.826
- [Audience] (whooping and applauding)

00:02:48.826 --> 00:02:50.190
- And that's not all.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:52.020
That's actually not all.
Our season-long partner

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:53.430
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:55.080
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson show,

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.750
they want to honor ultimate
overachievers just like you.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:02:59.040
So they're gonna be writing you a check

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:00.030
for a thousand dollars.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.030
How does that sound?

00:03:02.544 --> 00:03:05.259
- [Audience] (Whooping and applauding)

00:03:05.259 --> 00:03:06.104
- Oh my!

00:03:06.104 --> 00:03:06.937
- [Kelly Clarkson] I love it!

00:03:06.937 --> 00:03:08.301
- Thank you.

00:03:08.301 --> 00:03:09.134
Absolutely.

00:03:09.134 --> 00:03:09.967
Well, God bless you.

00:03:09.967 --> 00:03:10.800
Thank you so much for being an educator.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:11.960
We appreciate you.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:13.720
Thank you so much.

